@startuml 17-seq-browser-patch
!include _style.iuml
title The browser as client: forms in, HTML patches out

actor "Browser\n(no JS)" as b
participant "Server muppet\n(acts for this user)" as sm
participant "Host\n(session main)" as t
participant "Agent or\nother peer" as p

b -> sm : GET /host/doc@main (Accept: text/html)
sm --> b : 200 HTML: page, markers, handle popovers\n(response stays open: the patch stream)

== the user edits ==
b -> b : click the shape: its handle popover\nopens in the top layer (no request)
b -> sm : POST nudge form (node ID, snapshot,\nCSRF, request ID)
sm -> sm : resolve the edit (e.g. snap to grid),\nXmesh: CRDT op(s), apply
sm -> t : XTXP op (WebSocket)
sm --> b : 204 No Content (the page stays put)
sm --> b : stream: confirmation patch\n<template for="n7-12"> where it landed </template>\n<template for="status"> snapped to grid </template>
b -> b : browser applies the patch;\nview transition settles the shape

== someone else edits ==
p -> t : XTXP op
t -> sm : fan out op
sm -> sm : Xmesh integrate, re-render the node
sm --> b : stream: <template for="n9-3">…</template>
b -> b : patch applied; the change animates\n(styled by author: you, peer, agent)

note over sm
  All CRDT work stays in the muppet.
  The browser's own parser applies
  the patches: no client framework.
end note
@enduml
